Phasmid: speech synthesis voices

What:     speechSynthesis.getVoices() lists speech.voices in profile order
          (the first is the default) in place of the platform's. Each voice
          belongs to the unloaded "Google Network Speech" engine, so speak()
          gets no event until cancel(), as Google Chrome with its speech
          server unreachable. The host's speech-dispatcher is never used.
Why:      Google Chrome lists its network voices (and the local Microsoft
          voices on Windows); an ungoogled build lists none and has no API
          key to synthesize with.
Profile:  speech.voices
Hooks:    content/browser/speech/tts_controller_impl.cc
          TtsControllerImpl::GetVoices;
          content/browser/speech/tts_linux.cc TtsPlatformImplLinux constructor
Contexts: main, iframe; workers have no speechSynthesis
Guard:    tests/guards/platform/speech-voices.py

